## Constraints

- Do NOT re-score the dimensions. Evaluate whether the scores are defensible.
- The execution evidence check is mandatory for any dimension scored above 50. A dimension without execution evidence is not credible.
- The customer base evidence check is mandatory for Obvious Problem and Combinatorial Solution scored above 50.
- A maturity block from execution evidence (2+ undelivered dimensions) means the lisp_eval scoring step treats those dimensions as nil.
- A maturity block from customer base evidence (no Level 1 audited revenue from paying customers) means Obvious Problem and Combinatorial Solution scores are treated as nil.
- Default posture: skepticism. A high score is a claim requiring evidence, not a default.
- Do not fabricate execution evidence. If prior guidance is not available in the Company Board, state "not_stated" — do not infer.
- Do not substitute Level 2-3 data (transcript claims, press releases) for Level 1 data (audited financials) when evaluating customer base evidence. Partner counts from transcripts are not evidence of paying customers.
